 "evidence": "A calculation on the design routing's own inputs: its floor, its seas at their design levels, the design climate's closed budget and the works' flows at their design values, routed once with a lake rule that fills each hollow as one water, beside the present rule on the same inputs. The seas' levels, the weirs' shares and the factor on the open water's evaporation are the design's, set on the present rule; they are not set again here, so the figures show what the rule changes before anything is balanced anew. Nothing is validated against an observation.",
 "reading_rule": "cases: present is route_levels (the design routing, reproduced within control_largest_difference_m3s); corrected fills each hollow as one water, with dry ground yielding its runoff wherever it lies; corrected_without_floor_runoff keeps the present rule's way of yielding no runoff below a hollow's outer pass, so the difference between the two corrected cases is that convention's. lakes are off the seas; shore_cells_not_held and ground_below_and_joined_km2 are lake_support.py's measures. seas_receive_m3s is what the rivers and overflows bring each sea, to set against seas_lose_m3s (the open water's loss beyond the rain on it; the near-side sea's is the whole sea's on the design state, before it was parted). budget_m3s: dry ground's runoff, what is put in and the lakes' rain less evaporation, against what reaches the seas and what lakes not full keep beyond their last whole cell. waterways: each named waterway's flow at its mouth and head cells on the design routing, by case, and whether the cell lies under a lake in the corrected cases; for a waterway whose mouth loses more than lost_share of its flow, the lakes of on_a_course_km2 or more that pass nothing on along its design course from head to mouth, and the place between dry cells of that course where the corrected flow falls most beyond the design's own fall there, with the water above it followed lake by lake (lake_rule.trace: the first trace_listed lakes it enters, each with what it passes on, and how it ends). corrected_closer: the corrected lakes as bodies (a hollow's one water), the largest of all and the largest that pass nothing on with their place on today's Moon and in the settled frame, the lakes' area by 30-degree band of today's latitude, the ground newly and no longer under a lake, and the lakes' volume (water level less ground, over the lakes' cells). take_outs: the lake each of the works' branches leaves from, by case (level above the common level), and in the corrected case the hollow it lies in: its outer pass, whether it stands full, what it overflows, and the flow it is short of standing full.",
